    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 997,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Margaret Okayo\nMargaret Okayo ( born May 30 , 1976 in Masaba , Kisii District ) is a professional marathon runner from Kenya . She has won a number of major marathons , including the New York City Marathon ( three times ) , the Boston Marathon , and the London Marathon . She has also won the San Diego Marathon on two occasions . Okayo started running while at primary school . She graduated from the Itierio Secondary School , located near Kisii town , in 1993 . She was recruited by Kenya Prisons Service , home to the country 's top women 's marathon runners , in 1995 where she nurtured her running career . At the 1998 Commonwealth Games she finished fifth in 10,000 metres . She finished thirteenth at the 1999 IAAF World Half Marathon Championships . Amongst her most successful races are the wins at the New York Marathon in 2001 and 2003 , the Boston Marathon in 2002 and the London Marathon in 2004 . She still holds the course records at the New York Marathon and the Boston Marathon ."
     }
    ],
    "status": "ok"
   },
